{
  "name": "FOI Error Handler",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "f8f08c37-3b75-47d2-9622-95973923638f",
      "name": "FOI Error Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        816,
        384
      ],
      "notes": "Starts when FOI Request Routing or FOI Payment Expiry SLA Job fails (Settings > Error workflow). Sub-workflow failures bubble up to these two parents. Only automatic runs trigger it, not manual test runs."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Recipients come from the n8n variables foiErrorAlertEmails (To list) and foiErrorAlertFromEmail (sender).\n// n8n variables are always strings, so the list may be a JSON array ('[\"a@gov.bc.ca\",\"b@gov.bc.ca\"]')\n// or a comma/semicolon separated string. Invalid entries are dropped; an empty list skips the alert.\nconst raw = $vars.foiErrorAlertEmails;\nconst fromEmail = $vars.foiErrorAlertFromEmail;\nlet list = [];\nif (Array.isArray(raw)) {\n  list = raw;\n} else if (typeof raw === 'string' && raw.trim()) {\n  const text = raw.trim();\n  if (text.startsWith('[')) {\n    try { list = JSON.parse(text); } catch (e) { list = []; }\n  }\n  if (!Array.isArray(list) || list.length === 0) list = text.replace(/^\\[|\\]$/g, '').split(/[,;]/);\n}\nconst emails = [...new Set(list.map((e) => String(e).trim().replace(/^[\"']|[\"']$/g, '')).filter((e) => /^[^\\s@,;]+@[^\\s@,;]+\\.[^\\s@,;]+$/.test(e)))];\nreturn [{ json: { toEmail: emails.join(','), recipientCount: emails.length, fromEmail: String(fromEmail ?? '').trim() } }];"
      },
      "id": "2ce88706-e4fb-43c7-be81-0bae55afca20",
      "name": "Alert Recipients",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1040,
        384
      ],
      "notes": "Reads the n8n variables foiErrorAlertEmails (the To list: a JSON array string or comma separated) and foiErrorAlertFromEmail (sender). No recipients or no sender = the alert email is skipped; the failure is still recorded and the outbox row still marked FAILED."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Developer Overview – FOI Error Handler\n\n**Purpose:**\nMakes failed n8n runs visible. FOI Request Routing answers the API before it runs, so the API never sees a failure inside n8n. This workflow records the failure, marks the API outbox row FAILED (so it can be replayed) and alerts people.\n\n**Trigger/Entry:**\nError Trigger. Set as the **Error workflow** (workflow settings) of FOI Request Routing and FOI Payment Expiry SLA Job. Sub-workflow failures bubble up to those parents.\n\n**Processing:**\n1. Looks up `event_id` and the request ids with `GET /api/foiworkflow/executions/{id}/event` (through FOI Backend API Manager, `foi-event-by-execution`). The API outbox row knows the execution because FOI Request Routing recorded it when it claimed the event. It no longer reads `foi-process-audit`.\n2. Writes one row to the `foi-execution-errors` Data Table.\n3. If there is an `event_id`: calls `PUT /api/foiworkflow/events/{event_id}` with FAILED, the error and the failed execution id, through FOI Backend API Manager V2 (`foi-event-ack`).\n4. Sends one alert email (SMTP, credential `gov email smtp`) to every address in the n8n variable `foiErrorAlertEmails`, from `foiErrorAlertFromEmail`. `Alert Recipients` accepts a JSON array string or a comma separated list.\n\n**Integration/Outcome:**\nEvery step after the lookup continues on error, so one failing step never blocks the others. A run with no `event_id` (the SLA job, or a run that failed before the claim) is still recorded and alerted, just without an outbox update. If this workflow itself fails, nothing reports it: the API sweeper flags the outbox row as NO_OUTCOME after `N8N_OUTBOX_NO_OUTCOME_MINUTES`.\n\n**Setup:** run FOI - Initialize Data Tables, select `foi-execution-errors` in `Record Failure`, select the `gov email smtp` credential in `Send Alert Email`, create the variables `foiErrorAlertEmails` and `foiErrorAlertFromEmail`, then set this workflow as the Error workflow of the two parents.",
        "height": 700,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "363bd4b1-013c-4b06-ade7-2f0963a40703",
      "name": "Developer Overview1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
